Run-6 fixes for .claude/workflows/dead-code-discover-verify.js
==============================================================
.claude/ is gitignored (synced to the server via `make sync-claude`), so the
workflow script cannot be committed directly. This patch is the reviewable
record of the change; it is ALREADY APPLIED to the working copy on this host.

Apply elsewhere with:
    git apply audit/dead-code-workflow-fixes-run6.patch

Supersedes audit/dead-code-workflow-fixes.patch, which was never applied. Its
PROJECT/REPO env-var change is carried forward here; its Hard-Rule-6 addition
to the RULES block is included too.

What this changes
-----------------
1. PROJECT/REPO now read process.env.CBM_PROJECT / REPO_ROOT before falling
   back to this host's paths. Run 6 dispatched every lens with a macOS repo
   path and a codebase-memory project that does not exist here; all 7 lenses
   detected it and worked around it, at cost.
2. The RULES block no longer asserts the index is fresh at a hardcoded HEAD.
   Agents are told to confirm against the current HEAD and re-index if the
   graph disagrees with the working tree. Adds CLAUDE.md Hard Rule 6
   (/mem-search must query BOTH claude-mem projects).
3. normName() / keyOf() / lineKey() replace the raw `${file}::${name}`
   identity key at all 8 sites. Run 6's cascade round re-confirmed 6 items its
   own adversarial skeptic had refuted, because agents label the same symbol
   differently across rounds. normName strips trailing parentheticals and
   surrounding quotes, but keeps '"X" entry in pkg/__init__.py __all__'
   DISTINCT from X -- an __all__ string is a separate line to delete than its
   import, and collapsing them would silently drop one.
4. Cascade candidates are deduped against every ADJUDICATED item
   (all + confirmed + refuted + unsure + alive), not just the raw candidate
   set, so a refuted symbol can never re-enter. Also keys on file:start_line
   as a second identity, and logs how many candidates were dropped.

